1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:05,110
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers.]

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:05,460
What are you doing?

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:06,690
Where's Sungwoo?

4
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:07,890
He went home.

5
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:12,110
-What's wrong?
-I don't like this.

6
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,640
[CEO: Lee Won]

7
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,350
[Medical Expense
Settlement Statement/Receipt]

8
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:25,300
It seems you can't change
your bad habit of stealing.

9
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:33,870
You don't really think a few sheets
of music can keep Lee Hanyul, do you?

10
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,470
Tell me about it.

11
00:01:35,789 --> 00:01:38,050
I didn't expect it to be this easy either.

12
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:42,009
I just gave him a sheet of music,
and he left with me immediately.

13
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,420
You must be heartbroken.

14
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:48,970
Everyone has a past.

15
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,940
But he's by my side now.

16
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,890
Is it really just the past?

17
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:58,220
You...

18
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:02,840
Your impatience is the problem.

19
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:06,360
Going as far as breaking into my locker
to steal the music—

20
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,030
It's not really your place
to say that, is it?

21
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:11,160
It's all because you kept threatening him
for no reason.

22
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,500
I wasn't threatening him.

23
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:18,390
I was just helping him
come back to me faster.

24
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:26,070
Didn't you come here to get this back?

25
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:30,579
Ah, that?

26
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:33,640
This method won't last long anyway.

27
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:48,650
He clearly has a backup plan.

28
00:02:54,090 --> 00:03:00,750
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

29
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:06,700
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

30
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:09,460
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

31
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:12,390
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

32
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,480
[Yoo Dohyun]

33
00:03:30,490 --> 00:03:32,120
[Cho Chanhyeon]

34
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,750
[Ko Gyeol]

35
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:38,700
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

36
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,690
Oh, seriously.

37
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:50,390
What are you dissatisfied with now?

38
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:56,560
Did... Did something happen?

39
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:59,980
This guy hasn't been listening to me
for a while.

40
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:02,380
I didn't want to hit it...

41
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,660
Damn it.

42
00:04:03,830 --> 00:04:05,050
Boomboom!

43
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:06,620
Wake up!

44
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:10,210
How can a machine like you
change just like that?

45
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,380
You've changed.

46
00:04:12,550 --> 00:04:13,750
I'm sorry, Boomboom.

47
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,430
I hit you too hard.

48
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,720
It probably broke because
it's been used for too long.

49
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,959
It is quite old.

50
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:24,110
But I'm not ready to let it go yet.

51
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:26,920
I'm not mentally prepared, my Boomboom.

52
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:29,370
Is this... very expensive?

53
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:32,400
Boomboom... is worth this much.

54
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:33,900
Three million?

55
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,250
No, I mean Boomboom is worth this much.

56
00:04:36,409 --> 00:04:37,540
Thirty million?

57
00:04:37,659 --> 00:04:38,760
Yeah.

58
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,650
I'm sorry I made you unable
to take other jobs.

59
00:04:44,110 --> 00:04:46,730
What, are you planning
to buy me a new set?

60
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:49,900
No.

61
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,370
Don't listen.

62
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,490
Boomboom, don't listen.

63
00:04:56,050 --> 00:04:57,060
I'm sorry.

64
00:04:59,310 --> 00:05:00,470
Boomboom...

65
00:05:02,330 --> 00:05:03,550
Hello?

66
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,930
Is this Mr. Lee Hanyul?

67
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:09,400
This is the Talent Development Team
at Dawn Entertainment.

68
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:11,710
Look into my eyes.

69
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,420
Don't cry, Boomboom.

70
00:05:14,990 --> 00:05:16,690
Dawn Entertainment?

71
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,170
Boomboom...

72
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:23,780
I'm sorry...

73
00:05:24,050 --> 00:05:27,060
[Producer: Michelo]

74
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:46,630
Sorry, my meeting ended a bit late.

75
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:47,990
It's fine.

76
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,740
Have a seat.

77
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,820
I am...

78
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:59,030
Producer Michelo.

79
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,430
My name is Lee Hanyul.

80
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:04,410
What did you want to see me about?

81
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:07,900
Have you signed with an agency?

82
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,350
An agency?

83
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:12,540
I haven't signed... with any.

84
00:06:12,770 --> 00:06:14,050
What about a manager?

85
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:16,650
I don't have a manager either.

86
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:18,320
Is that so?

87
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,120
I heard our Team Leader Ko

88
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:26,250
left you a business card
at the Sandol Village festival.

89
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,790
You never contacted us,

90
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:31,990
but recently, someone related to you
called us.

91
00:06:32,210 --> 00:06:33,870
Someone related to me?

92
00:06:34,570 --> 00:06:36,020
Who could it be...

93
00:06:37,490 --> 00:06:39,330
I'm not too sure who that could be,

94
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:41,330
but I do have a teacher.

95
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:42,900
A teacher?

96
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,100
Yes.

97
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:47,159
His name is Mr. Pan.
He gives me vocal lessons.

98
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:49,710
Pan?

99
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,880
Yes. Do you know him?

100
00:07:01,450 --> 00:07:03,980
Let's not go around in circles.

101
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,850
Sign with our agency.

102
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:09,000
I've seen your videos.

103
00:07:09,130 --> 00:07:10,600
I'll help you debut.

104
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:13,060
Also, whatever conditions you want,

105
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,510
I can satisfy them.

106
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,470
Is there anything you want?

107
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:26,010
Boomboom... is worth this much.

108
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:27,080
Three million?

109
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:29,360
No, I mean Boomboom is worth this much.

110
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:30,690
Thirty million?

111
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:34,630
I'd like to get the signing bonus first.

112
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:35,930
Okay.

113
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:39,760
Also, there's a song
I really want to sing.

114
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:41,560
A song you really want to sing?

115
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:43,110
Yes.

116
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:45,740
I want to debut with this song.

117
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,490
Sure.

118
00:07:47,650 --> 00:07:49,850
We can consider this later.

119
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:05,900
Then let's release a remake album
of old songs first.

120
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:09,230
We'll start recording tomorrow.

121
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,210
Tomorrow? That fast?

122
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,520
What's wrong?

123
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:16,320
I'm sure that teacher
must've trained you well.

124
00:08:16,670 --> 00:08:17,710
Ah...

125
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:21,830
Sign it.

126
00:08:24,550 --> 00:08:26,520
Right... Right now?

127
00:08:32,570 --> 00:08:35,720
[Article 5: Breach of Artist Obligations and Test Content
Article 6: Prohibition of Using External Songs and Leakage of Sound Sources
Article 7: Profit Distribution and Settlement]

128
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:38,130
The signing bonus
can be transferred to you today.

129
00:08:40,950 --> 00:08:43,669
One, two, three, four...

130
00:08:44,169 --> 00:08:45,370
One hundred million?

131
00:08:45,410 --> 00:08:47,890
What, is it not enough?

132
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:49,590
No.

133
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,280
The sooner the better.

134
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:00,740
That way you can debut
as soon as possible.

135
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:03,770
But this fast is still a bit...

136
00:09:04,350 --> 00:09:05,540
Ah.

137
00:09:05,970 --> 00:09:08,160
You just asked me if I knew Pan, right?

138
00:09:08,450 --> 00:09:09,600
Yes.

139
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,370
He's my friend.

140
00:09:11,530 --> 00:09:13,080
An old friend of many years.

141
00:09:13,650 --> 00:09:15,070
Really?

142
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:19,030
That's why I proposed
to sign as soon as possible.

143
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:22,830
His beloved student
must have reliable skills.

144
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:32,570
I have another appointment next.

145
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:35,240
If you don't want to sign,
you don't have to.

146
00:09:35,890 --> 00:09:37,210
I'll sign.

147
00:09:55,450 --> 00:09:56,550
Good.

148
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,910
See you at the recording tomorrow.

149
00:09:58,910 --> 00:09:59,730
Okay.

150
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:00,850
Ah.

151
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,470
If it's convenient,
you can invite your teacher along.

152
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:07,620
It would give me a rare chance to see him.

153
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:09,710
Thank you.

154
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:12,370
Thank you!

155
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:25,620
Where is Lee Hanyul?

156
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,240
I don't know.

157
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:29,170
I saw him answer a call and go out.

158
00:10:29,710 --> 00:10:30,550
A call?

159
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,460
Dusk...

160
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:34,520
Dusk Entertainment or something.

161
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,860
There's no such entertainment company.

162
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,940
Why would an entertainment company
look for him?

163
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:42,130
I don't know.
It's probably a phishing scam.

164
00:10:52,770 --> 00:10:53,810
What...

165
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:57,180
-Hey!
-Help me.

166
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,810
Hey, what...

167
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,300
What is this?

168
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:06,070
Gah!

169
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:07,560
Could... Could this be?

170
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:11,030
This is a gift to thank you, Mr. Pan.

171
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:16,200
You're not the victim of a phishing scam,
but you scammed someone else instead?

172
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,880
It's not like that.

173
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:22,910
You brat.

174
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,670
Boomboom...

175
00:11:28,810 --> 00:11:30,200
My Boomboom...

176
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:37,610
So...

177
00:11:38,810 --> 00:11:41,140
Where did you get
such a large sum of money?

178
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:42,700
It's a secret.

179
00:11:44,810 --> 00:11:45,860
Hey.

180
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,790
Do you know how expensive this thing is?

181
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:51,370
I know. I bought it.

182
00:11:54,230 --> 00:11:55,690
Hehe.

183
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,420
You are the new Boomboom.

184
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,780
New Boomboom.

185
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:03,320
I want to debut as soon as possible
to pay off the favors I owe,

186
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,890
to pay off what I owe Mr. Pan.

187
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:07,700
Boomboom, hehe.

188
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:15,750
And pay off what I owe you.

189
00:12:17,830 --> 00:12:20,350
I'll be able to sing your songs soon too.

190
00:12:32,650 --> 00:12:33,750
Don't be nervous.

191
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:35,840
Just sing with a relaxed mind.

192
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,190
Okay.

193
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:39,920
Drink this.

194
00:12:40,370 --> 00:12:41,580
Thank you.

195
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,630
Can you hear me?

196
00:13:11,850 --> 00:13:14,810
Give me a signal when you're ready.

197
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:25,730
Okay.

198
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,180
Here it comes.

199
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,020
Play the MR.

200
00:14:18,830 --> 00:14:23,350
How could you sign the contract
knowing you had a problem with your voice?

201
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:30,450
You have an obligation to seriously cooperate
with the company for the designated tests.

202
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:33,170
If the project is halted
due to the signing party's own reasons,

203
00:14:33,170 --> 00:14:35,960
the company has the right
to recover the initial investment and losses,

204
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:39,180
and all expenses must be
fully refunded to the agency.

205
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:39,150
[Must be fully refunded to the agency.]

206
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:43,820
Recording engineers,

207
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:44,950
the manpower responsible for you,

208
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:46,310
and preparations—

209
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,750
all of these cost money.

210
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:58,690
Now, because you breached the contract,
both parties are terminating it.

211
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:00,170
[Indictment]

212
00:14:58,990 --> 00:15:00,050
As for the penalty,

213
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:02,820
I will thoroughly discuss it
with the legal team

214
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,790
and let you know later.

215
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:06,480
Hanyul!

216
00:15:11,890 --> 00:15:15,920
Wow, friend, long time no see.

217
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,060
[Indictment]

218
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:25,400
Bastard...

219
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,600
Stop!

220
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:31,280
Take Hanyul away.

221
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,140
This is my problem.

222
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,970
Let's go.

223
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:48,170
How did you...

224
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,810
You want to ask why we knew?

225
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:52,000
It's because you act too weirdly.

226
00:15:54,650 --> 00:15:55,980
Don't speak.

227
00:15:58,510 --> 00:16:00,210
Thankfully we managed
to treat it soon enough,

228
00:16:00,210 --> 00:16:03,040
so the vocal cords
are not completely damaged.

229
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:04,410
As long as he doesn't overuse his voice,

230
00:16:04,410 --> 00:16:05,610
he will recover soon.

231
00:16:05,770 --> 00:16:06,960
Okay, thank you.

232
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:07,920
Sure.

233
00:16:15,450 --> 00:16:17,320
Did he give you anything?

234
00:16:21,930 --> 00:16:23,190
Pan

235
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:26,200
used to be the lead singer
of a very popular group...

236
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,980
in the same group as Michelo.

237
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:50,040
What?

238
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,990
Are you going to kneel before me?

239
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:04,609
What's going on?

240
00:17:05,210 --> 00:17:07,470
Pan is past his prime.

241
00:17:10,109 --> 00:17:12,700
Please don't touch Hanyul.

242
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:17,560
The contract and the penalty—

243
00:17:18,530 --> 00:17:20,560
let's just pretend it never happened.

244
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,660
I'm begging you as a friend.

245
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:31,650
Do you think begging me will solve it?

246
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:41,540
Do you know why I hate you so much?

247
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:48,240
You always look at me with pity.

248
00:17:50,230 --> 00:17:56,410
I tried my best just to
stand by your side in this life.

249
00:17:56,970 --> 00:17:59,860
But you never saw me as a rival.

250
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:04,170
I thought we were on the same team.

251
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:07,580
That's exactly it!

252
00:18:07,870 --> 00:18:10,510
That's the most disgusting part. Damn it.

253
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:13,430
Hey, I...

254
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,920
did everything I could to beat you.

255
00:18:16,050 --> 00:18:18,020
But you didn't even consider me a rival.

256
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:21,950
You just thought of me
as your useless sidekick, right?

257
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,120
The contract?

258
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,400
Fine.

259
00:18:29,890 --> 00:18:31,840
Let's pretend it never happened.

260
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:38,500
But...

261
00:18:57,350 --> 00:18:59,840
What's going on?

262
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:02,080
Were you waiting for me?

263
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:04,010
Shh.

264
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:06,300
Don't say anything.

265
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:08,320
You can't speak anyway.

266
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:09,460
Don't worry, kid.

267
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:12,190
I've taken care of everything.

268
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:18,680
What is this?

269
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:26,490
I wanted to help you and Lee Won.

270
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:34,380
[I wanted to help you and Lee Won. But I didn't even discuss it with you,
and foolishly signed the contract. I feel so stupid.]

271
00:19:26,610 --> 00:19:27,960
But I didn't even discuss it with you,

272
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:30,830
and foolishly signed the contract.

273
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,710
I feel so stupid.

274
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:41,910
[It's my fault you had to go through such a terrible thing. I messed everything up.
You worked so hard for me, and it's all my fault. I'm sorry, I'm really sorry.]

275
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:45,310
Oh, you brat.

276
00:19:45,450 --> 00:19:47,490
What did you do wrong?

277
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,090
It's just old geezers
trying to satisfy their own desires.

278
00:19:50,090 --> 00:19:53,030
Why are you putting yourself down, brat?

279
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:54,600
It's okay, kid.

280
00:19:55,510 --> 00:19:56,580
Hey.

281
00:19:57,210 --> 00:20:00,320
Speaking of, you type really fast.

282
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,360
You're quite capable.

283
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:04,730
You don't even need to speak.

284
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:10,460
I'm taking him away today.

285
00:20:10,770 --> 00:20:12,370
Go out first.

286
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:16,940
Hey.

287
00:20:17,690 --> 00:20:21,740
The dangerous one for Hanyul
isn't Michelo,

288
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:23,900
but you.

289
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:25,370
Are you okay?

290
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:27,670
What do you mean?

291
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,620
Nothing happened.

292
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,880
What exactly happened?

293
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:39,110
Give me the copyrights
to all the songs under your name.

294
00:20:39,670 --> 00:20:40,980
Also,

295
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:43,950
whatever songs you write in the future

296
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:49,300
must be registered under my name.

297
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:52,470
You...

298
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:56,160
will be my ghostwriter
for the rest of your life.

299
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,080
Okay.

300
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,050
Let's do that, friend.

301
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:14,070
Maybe she still thinks I'm a genius.

302
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:16,500
That I just need to write songs for her.

303
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:19,810
We're all friends.
We've cleared things up.

304
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:23,170
Gosh, she really liked me.

305
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:25,790
But it's a pity.

306
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:29,340
I was planning to make a fortune off
Hanyul's good voice.

307
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,930
Seriously.

308
00:21:31,430 --> 00:21:32,360
Tsk.

309
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:33,770
What's wrong?

310
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:36,690
What...

311
00:21:36,810 --> 00:21:38,010
What's your issue?

312
00:21:45,430 --> 00:21:46,650
Blow your nose.

313
00:22:03,210 --> 00:22:04,330
Here.

314
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,460
Done.

315
00:22:10,310 --> 00:22:13,240
I look so stupid, right?

316
00:22:14,030 --> 00:22:15,860
You're not stupid.

317
00:22:18,980 --> 00:22:21,710
I should have killed that woman earlier.

318
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,370
Lee Hanyul.

319
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:35,620
Do you still want to sing?

320
00:22:38,790 --> 00:22:39,880
There we go.

321
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:41,220
Stop crying.

322
00:22:41,990 --> 00:22:43,610
Go wash up and go to sleep.

323
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,870
All right.

324
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:14,610
Hanyul.

325
00:23:19,490 --> 00:23:21,650
Whether it's in the past or now,

326
00:23:24,730 --> 00:23:27,140
you did nothing wrong.

327
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:35,570
So you don't have to run away,

328
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,470
and you don't have to cry.

329
00:23:46,020 --> 00:23:47,890
Don't cry.

330
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:57,120
When you cry, I don't know what to do.

331
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:13,240
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

332
00:27:13,260 --> 00:27:14,400
Hey, fire!

333
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:15,930
Fire! Fire!

334
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:17,330
Hmm?

335
00:27:17,490 --> 00:27:18,350
I am an idiot.

336
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:20,680
So until your voice goes back to normal,

337
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:22,240
I'll continue to be an idiot.

338
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,570
It's finally done—

339
00:27:23,810 --> 00:27:25,520
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

340
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,140
the song I want to give you.

341
00:27:25,140 --> 00:27:27,490
Adolph... is gone.

342
00:27:27,730 --> 00:27:28,660
What did you say?

343
00:27:28,660 --> 00:27:29,650
It's true.

344
00:27:29,810 --> 00:27:31,410
I really have been taking care of him.

345
00:27:31,410 --> 00:27:33,240
Here, are you satisfied now?

346
00:27:33,460 --> 00:27:35,780
Just kill me. I beg you to just kill me!

347
00:27:39,040 --> 00:27:40,460
Who are you?
